    <!-- General panel -->
    <sys:String x:Key="L.General.Title">⚙ General Settings</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.General.Subtitle">Core settings for EVE MultiPreview hotkey behavior.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.General.ShowTimer">Show Session Timer on Thumbnails</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.General.HotkeyScope">Hotkey Scope</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.General.ActivationScope">Activation scope:</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.General.ScopeGlobal">Global</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.General.ScopeEveActive">If an EVE window is Active</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.General.HotkeyWildcard">Hotkeys still fire while Ctrl / Shift / Alt is held</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.General.HotkeyWildcardNote">On: a hotkey works even while you hold a modifier — EVE players hold Ctrl to lock targets. Off: a single-key hotkey such as V only fires on its own, so Ctrl+V reaches the client for pasting.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.General.PropagateModifiers">Carry held Ctrl / Shift / Alt to the client you switch to</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.General.PropagateModifiersNote">On: holding Ctrl to lock a target keeps working after you cycle to another client. Turn it off if locking stops working after a switch — on some setups the client already sees the held key and these extra keystrokes get in the way.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.General.PropagateKeys">Carry other held keys to the client you switch to</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.General.PropagateKeysNote">On: letters, numbers, F-keys, Enter, Space and mouse buttons you are still holding when you switch are pressed in the new client too (hold F1 and cycle to fire it on each). Turn it off if a module key you have not released yet activates on the next client and your own press then turns it back off. Held Ctrl / Shift / Alt follow the setting above.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.General.HideHeldKeys">Hide keys you're still holding from the client you switch to</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.General.HideHeldKeysNote">For letters, numbers, F-keys, Enter and Space. A key still down when you switch is released in the client you leave and kept away from the one you land on until you let go, so holding A (align) or S (warp) can't make the next client align or warp. Takes priority over “Carry other held keys”. Ctrl / Shift / Alt are never hidden: they follow their own option above, and hiding them would break held-modifier hotkeys such as Ctrl+TAB.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.General.HideHotkeyKeystrokes">Hide hotkey keystrokes from EVE (as EVE-X-Preview does)</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.General.HideHotkeyKeystrokesNote">On: when a hotkey switches clients, the client you land on never sees that key. Off: the key's release reaches that client, which can make your first click there only focus EVE's overview instead of acting.</sys:String>
