    <!-- Performance panel -->
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Perf.Title">⚡ CPU Performance &amp; Affinity</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Perf.Subtitle">Orchestrate CPU priority and core affinity to ensure inactive clients never steal P-Core cycles.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Perf.GlobalSettings">Global Settings</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Perf.ManageAffinity">Enable Background Client Affinity/Priority Management</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Perf.ManageAffinityNote">When enabled, inactive EVE clients are dropped to 'Idle' priority to prevent stuttering.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Perf.AutoBalance">Auto-Balance Inactive Clients to E-Cores (App Decides)</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Perf.AutoBalanceNote">Dynamically round-robins inactive clients across the bottom half of your logical cores (E-Cores or 2nd CCD).</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Perf.GpuOpt">Thumbnail GPU Optimization</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Perf.LowGpuBtn">⚡ Optimize for Low GPU (recommended for many clients)</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Perf.LowGpuNote">One click: minimizes inactive clients on switch AND suspends background thumbnails, so idle clients stop rendering entirely. The single biggest FPS / fan-noise win when multiboxing many clients.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Perf.StaticThumbs">Static Thumbnails (lower GPU)</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Perf.StaticThumbsNote">Replaces the live DWM-composited preview with a snapshot refreshed roughly once per second. Big GPU saving when running many clients (DWM no longer composites every frame), at the cost of choppy motion — ship movement updates on the snapshot cadence instead of smoothly. Best for fleets where you only need to glance at thumbnails occasionally rather than watch them constantly.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Perf.SuspendBg">Suspend Thumbnails When Background</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Perf.SuspendBgNote">Freezes every thumbnail to its last frame whenever neither EVE nor MultiPreview is the foreground process. Resumes live composition the moment EVE or the app comes back. Invisible during active play; stops the GPU paying for thumbnails of windows you can't see while you're working in another app. Adds a sub-second wakeup lag when you alt-tab back.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Perf.CoreOverrides">Per-Client Core Overrides</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Perf.CoreOverridesNote">Explicitly force a specific character to a specific logical processor when they are INACTIVE. This overrides Auto-Balance.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Perf.ColInactiveCore">Inactive Core</sys:String>

