    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Opt.StartupMinimized">Open settings minimized</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.app.general.startWithWindows">Start with Windows</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.app.general.startWithWindows.Desc">Launch MultiPreview to the tray when you sign in to Windows.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.app.general.Intro">Choose the language, how big this window is, and what MultiPreview does when Windows starts.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.app.general.language.Title">Language and size</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.app.general.language.Body">**Automatic** uses your Windows display language when MultiPreview has it, and English otherwise.&#x0A;&#x0A;Translations other than English were drafted by machine. If something reads wrong, say so on GitHub and it gets fixed in the next release.&#x0A;&#x0A;**Settings window size** only changes this window, not the thumbnails.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.app.general.startup.Title">Starting with Windows</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.app.general.startup.Body">**Start with Windows** launches MultiPreview to the tray when you sign in.&#x0A;&#x0A;**When MultiPreview starts** decides whether this window opens too. Choose minimized to have it ready on the taskbar without covering EVE.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.app.look.Intro">Pick how MultiPreview's windows look. The look is the same in every profile.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.app.look.look.Title">Looks</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.app.look.look.Body">Each card shows a small preview of a look; one click picks it. The settings window, its dialogs, the menus and the alerts change at once; nothing has to restart. The thumbnails and their text stay as they are.&#x0A;&#x0A;**Classic** is the navy of the old settings window. **Windows 11** is the dark look of Windows 11's own Settings. **High contrast** is black and white, with larger text. The other nine have their own colours and type, and **Capsule**, **Blueprint**, **Ink** and **Terminal** also lay out the page their own way.&#x0A;&#x0A;With the keyboard, Tab comes to the card of the look in use, the arrow keys move between the cards, and Space or Enter picks one.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Page.app.diagnostics">Diagnostics</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Page.app.diagnostics.Desc">Debug logs for tracking down a problem.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Sec.app.diagnostics.logs">Debug logs</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.app.diagnostics.note">Leave these off unless you're reporting a bug. Each one writes its own file in the Logs folder, and some write a lot.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.app.diagnostics.injection">Key and click sending</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.app.diagnostics.injection.Desc">Keys and clicks MultiPreview sends to your clients.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.app.diagnostics.cycling">Client switching</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.app.diagnostics.cycling.Desc">Every switching hotkey and the client it picked.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.app.diagnostics.windowHooks">Window events</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.app.diagnostics.windowHooks.Desc">Client windows opening, moving, getting focus and closing.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.app.diagnostics.dwm">Thumbnail drawing</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.app.diagnostics.dwm.Desc">How Windows draws the live thumbnails.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.app.diagnostics.alerts">Alerts</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.app.diagnostics.alerts.Desc">Lines read from the EVE logs and the alerts they triggered.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.app.diagnostics.folder">Log files</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Act.app.diagnostics.openLogs">Open logs folder</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.app.diagnostics.Intro">Debug logs help track down a problem. Turn on only the one you're asked for, make the problem happen, then turn it off and send the file.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.app.diagnostics.logs.Title">Which log to turn on</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.app.diagnostics.logs.Body">- **Key and click sending**: keys reaching the wrong client, or modifier keys that stick.&#x0A;- **Client switching**: hotkeys that skip a client or switch to the wrong one.&#x0A;- **Window events**: thumbnails that don't appear, or follow the wrong window.&#x0A;- **Thumbnail drawing**: black or frozen thumbnails.&#x0A;- **Alerts**: alerts that fire when they shouldn't, or not at all.&#x0A;&#x0A;The **Alerts** log names the character of each alert and every running character; with **Alerts** off none of that is written.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Page.app.profiles">Profiles &amp; backups</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Page.app.profiles.Desc">Switch, copy and back up your setups.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Sec.app.profiles.profiles">Profiles</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.app.profiles.current">Current profile</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.app.profiles.current.Desc">Each profile keeps its own thumbnail positions, hotkeys, colours and layout.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Sec.app.profiles.backups">Backups</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.app.profiles.backup">Settings file</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.app.profiles.backup.Desc">Backups go to the Backups folder in your settings folder. MultiPreview also keeps a copy when it starts, if your settings changed since the last one (the last 10). Export and import move your settings to another PC.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Act.app.profiles.backupNow">Back up now</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Act.app.profiles.export">Export…</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Act.app.profiles.import">Import…</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.app.profiles.Intro">A profile is a complete setup: where thumbnails sit, hotkeys, colours, crops and client layout. Keep one per activity, like mining and PvP.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.app.profiles.profiles.Title">Working with profiles</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.app.profiles.profiles.Body">- **New** starts an empty profile and switches to it.&#x0A;- **Copy** copies one profile into another: everything, or only thumbnail positions.&#x0A;- **Delete** removes the current profile for good. You always keep at least one.&#x0A;- **Copy look as code** puts the look of the current profile (borders, text, opacity, when thumbnails hide) on the clipboard as one line of text; **New profile from a code…** makes a copy of the current profile with that look. A look code carries no character names, positions or hotkeys.&#x0A;- **Copy profile code with characters** also carries the names of the characters the profile knows and what the profile keeps for each: positions and sizes, visibility, colours, labels, second thumbnails, crops, client positions, the never-minimize and excluded lists, membership of slots, cycle groups, colour groups and thumbnail groups, and the characters that pick the profile. It never carries hotkeys, CPU cores, audio volumes or statistics, and a code never sets a hotkey. **New profile from a code…** asks which of your characters each character in the code is (the same name is pre-selected; “(skip)” leaves one out), then makes a copy of the current profile in which those characters get the code's data; Cancel makes nothing. Positions are screen pixels and fit best on a similar monitor setup.&#x0A;- **Compare with…** goes through the settings that differ from another profile one by one, so you can take its value or keep yours; nothing is written to the other profile, and the startup backups are the undo.&#x0A;&#x0A;You can also switch from the profile menu at the top left, or with the profile hotkeys.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.app.profiles.backups.Title">Backups and moving to another PC</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.app.profiles.backups.Body">**Back up now** saves a dated copy in the Backups folder. MultiPreview also keeps a copy when it starts, if your settings changed since the last one (the last 10), and one before every update. If your settings file can't be read or is missing, it offers these copies when it starts.&#x0A;&#x0A;**Export** saves your settings file wherever you like. **Import** replaces all your settings with an exported file. Your current settings are backed up first.&#x0A;&#x0A;Your settings are normally kept in %APPDATA%\EVE MultiPreview. To keep them beside MultiPreview.exe instead (a portable install), close MultiPreview, copy your settings file there, and put an empty file named portable.txt beside the exe.</sys:String>
