    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Sec.app.general.control">Other programs</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.app.general.acceptCommands">Take commands from other programs</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.app.general.acceptCommands.Desc">Lets a Stream Deck, AutoHotkey or a shortcut tell the running MultiPreview to bring a character to the front, switch profile, or toggle thumbnails or focus mode. Only programs of your own Windows account can.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Msg.CommandsOff">EVE MultiPreview is already running but did not take the command. Turn on Take commands from other programs under App settings › General. If MultiPreview runs as administrator, turn on Also take commands from programs that are not run as administrator there, or run this program as administrator too. Otherwise try again once MultiPreview has finished starting.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.app.general.commands.Title">Commands from other programs</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.app.general.commands.Body">With **Take commands from other programs** on, starting MultiPreview again with one of these commands hands it to the MultiPreview that is running, and the second start ends at once:&#x0A;&#x0A;- --focus "Character name" brings that character's client to the front, as a click on its thumbnail does.&#x0A;- --cycle "Group name" and --cycle-back "Group name" go to the next or previous running character of that group, as the group's keys do.&#x0A;- --cycle-all and --cycle-all-back go to the next or previous client of all of them.&#x0A;- --previous-client goes back to the client you used before this one.&#x0A;- --last-alert goes to the client behind the alert that needs you.&#x0A;- --profile "Profile name" switches to that profile; --next-profile and --previous-profile step through the profiles.&#x0A;- --toggle-thumbnails hides or shows all thumbnails.&#x0A;- --focus-mode turns focus mode on or off (Clients › Groups).&#x0A;- --do-not-disturb turns do-not-disturb on or off.&#x0A;- --do-not-disturb-on and --do-not-disturb-off, --focus-mode-on and --focus-mode-off set exactly that state and do nothing if it is already there, so a button never drifts out of step.&#x0A;- --mute "Character name" mutes that running character's alerts for 1 hour, the longest timed length on a thumbnail's right-click menu; --unmute "Character name" ends the mute. A character that is not running ends with 2.&#x0A;&#x0A;A Stream Deck, Touch Portal, AutoHotkey or a Windows shortcut can run them. One command per start; anything else is refused. The second start ends with 0 when it was done, 1 when it was refused, 2 when there is no such character, group or profile, and 3 when no MultiPreview took it.&#x0A;&#x0A;Only programs running under your own Windows account can send commands, nothing is listened for on the network, and a command never names a file. MultiPreview and the program that sends must both run as administrator, or neither, unless you turn on **Also take commands from programs that are not run as administrator** (see When MultiPreview runs as administrator). A MultiPreview started with a command runs it once it has started, whatever this switch says.</sys:String>
