    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.thumbs.layout.align.Title">Align, distribute and nudge</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.thumbs.layout.align.Body">Tick the characters whose thumbnails you want to arrange; the list shows the characters that are logged in. Then press a button.&#x0A;&#x0A;- **Align left**, **Align right**, **Align top** and **Align bottom** line the ticked thumbnails up on that edge. The outermost one stays where it is.&#x0A;- **Space evenly across** and **Space evenly down** need three or more. The two outermost stay and the ones between are spread with equal gaps.&#x0A;- **Match width** and **Match height** give every ticked thumbnail the size of the first one you ticked. With **Keep the shape when resizing** on, each keeps its own shape and the other side follows.&#x0A;- The arrow buttons move the ticked thumbnails by 1 or 10 pixels; one thumbnail is enough.&#x0A;&#x0A;A thumbnail never leaves its screen: one that would is pulled back. Every action is one step for Undo (below), and the places are saved in this profile. Thumbnails never take the keyboard, so there is no arrow-key nudge: use the arrow buttons.</sys:String>
