    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.thumbs.text.streamer">Streamer mode</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.thumbs.text.streamer.Desc">Keeps what could give you away off a stream or a screenshot: character names show as Client 1, Client 2 and so on, and labels and system names are left out. Off by default.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.thumbs.text.streamer.Title">Streamer mode</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.thumbs.text.streamer.Body">**Streamer mode** keeps what could give you away off a stream or a screenshot. A character name is drawn as Client 1, Client 2 and so on, numbered in the order MultiPreview first sees the names after it starts. Labels and system names are left out.&#x0A;&#x0A;It covers the text on thumbnails (second thumbnails and crop windows too), the stats windows, the quick-switch wheel, the thumbnail right-click menu, the alert history window and the image you can save of a layout (its names are then always hidden). Only what is drawn changes: your settings, alerts and snoozes still go by the real names.&#x0A;&#x0A;It also covers the toasts and their menu, Windows notifications, spoken alerts, the notes that appear near the pointer, the profile and second-thumbnail lists in the tray menu and the downtime balloon. In those notes a group, profile or layout name reads Group 1, Profile 1 or Layout 1. The Discord message leaves your PC as text, so it carries Client 1 and never the real name. You can switch the mode on and off from the tray menu.&#x0A;&#x0A;It cannot hide the picture of the EVE client inside a thumbnail, or the names in this settings window. Keep the settings window off the stream.</sys:String>
