    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.thumbs.text.template">Text template</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.thumbs.text.template.Desc">Builds the text on a thumbnail from {name}, {system}, {timer}, {label}, {jumps} and {week}, for example {name} · {system}. Empty shows them as separate lines.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Opt.TemplateExamples">Fill in an example</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.thumbs.text.template.Title">Text template</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.thumbs.text.template.Body">**Text template** builds the text on a thumbnail from six pieces: {name} is the character name, {system} the solar system, {timer} the session timer, {label} the label you gave the character and {jumps} the number of jumps the character has made since MultiPreview started. Cyno, wormhole and clone jumps count as jumps; the first system MultiPreview sees the character in does not. Type them with anything in between, for example {name} · {system} or {label} {name} {timer}, or pick an example from the list. {week} is the character's playtime of the last seven days, like 14 h or 2 h 5 m; it shows nothing unless Count playtime per character is on.&#x0A;&#x0A;A piece with nothing to show takes the separators next to it away, so a thumbnail without a label does not start with a dangling dot. A piece whose switch above is off is left out the same way. Anything else in braces stays as you typed it; to show a brace itself, type it twice. A template can be up to 120 characters; a longer one is cut.&#x0A;&#x0A;The whole text uses the colour, font and size of the character name, and streamer mode still applies inside it. The template is used on the main thumbnails; other windows that show a name keep showing just the name. Leave it empty to keep the separate lines.</sys:String>
