    <sys:String x:Key="L.Palette.Kind.Label">Label of {0}</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Palette.Kind.Group">Group</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Palette.Kind.Profile">Profile</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.clients.hotkeys.palette.Title">The command palette</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.clients.hotkeys.palette.Body">With 20 clients or more, typing is faster than aiming. **Open the command palette** shows a small box over the monitor your mouse is on.&#x0A;&#x0A;- Type a few letters of a character, a label, a group or a profile. Each word you type must start a word of the name, or appear in it.&#x0A;- Up and Down choose a row, Enter runs it. With nothing typed, the box lists your running characters.&#x0A;- A character or a label brings that client forward, as clicking its thumbnail does. A group cycles forward, as its key does. A profile switches to that profile.&#x0A;- Esc, a click away from the box, or the key again closes it.&#x0A;&#x0A;Pick a key with Ctrl, Alt or Shift: a plain letter would keep you from typing it. While hotkeys are paused, its key does nothing. With streamer mode on, the list shows the masked names and leaves labels out.</sys:String>
    <!-- Ideas batch 19 (Plan 23) -->
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Sec.app.diagnostics.playtime">Weekly playtime</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.app.diagnostics.trackPlaytime">Count playtime per character</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.app.diagnostics.trackPlaytime.Desc">Adds up how long each character's client is open, day by day, so a thumbnail text template can show {week}. Off by default: it keeps character names in a file (playtime.json) in your settings folder. That file is never part of a bug report or of a code you share.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.app.diagnostics.playtimeHistory">Playtime history</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.app.diagnostics.playtimeHistory.Desc">Deletes the file with every character's counted playtime, and the totals the running app holds.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Act.app.diagnostics.clearPlaytime">Clear playtime history</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Act.app.diagnostics.clearPlaytime.Confirm">Delete the playtime counted for every character? This can't be undone.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Playtime.Cleared">Playtime history cleared.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.app.diagnostics.playtime.Title">Weekly playtime</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.app.diagnostics.playtime.Body">**Count playtime per character** adds up how long each character's client is open, day by day, and keeps the last two weeks. Put {week} in the text template of the thumbnails to show the last seven days, for example 14 h or 2 h 5 m.&#x0A;&#x0A;It is off by default, because it keeps character names in a file, playtime.json, in your settings folder. The file is saved every five minutes and when MultiPreview closes. It is never part of a bug report or of a code you share, and with the switch off nothing is read or written and {week} shows nothing.&#x0A;&#x0A;A character counts while its thumbnail exists, whether or not you are playing it. **Clear playtime history** deletes the file and the totals at once. Forgetting a character removes it from the file as well.&#x0A;&#x0A;Both **Clear playtime history** and forgetting a character also work with the switch off, and then open the file even though nothing else does. If you move your settings between the portable folder and AppData, the old playtime.json stays behind, and Clear only removes the one in the folder in use.</sys:String>
